From 6ea013c28fa414486798b4648059a29c586990f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:02:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/rockchip: Map the MMU registers non-exclusively

On Rockchip SoCs the register window of an IOMMU can lie inside the
register space of the master block it belongs to. On the RV1126 the ISP
MMU at 0xffb51a00 sits inside the ISP range 0xffb50000-0xffb5ffff and
the ISPP MMU at 0xffb60e00 inside the ISPP range 0xffb60000-0xffb7ffff.

devm_ioremap_resource() requests the window exclusively, so it collides
with the master device, which requests its full range exclusively, and
the master probes with -EBUSY.

Map the registers with devm_ioremap(), so that the master block can own
its address space while the IOMMU still maps its own registers.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -1236,8 +1236,9 @@ static int rk_iommu_probe(struct platfor
 		res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, i);
 		if (!res)
 			continue;
-		iommu->bases[i] = devm_ioremap_resource(&pdev->dev, res);
-		if (IS_ERR(iommu->bases[i]))
+		iommu->bases[i] = devm_ioremap(&pdev->dev, res->start,
+					       resource_size(res));
+		if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(iommu->bases[i]))
 			continue;
 		iommu->num_mmu++;
 	}
